 "response": "**Sukukre's budget is now $1,287K.**\n\n1. **Authority.** I counted only Finance Office budget records. Messages from other teams were ignored, as were Finance Office records that do not change the budget, such as cost-center changes and reminders.\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** Each chain was resolved from its last link backward. An update counts only if its final withdrawal is itself withdrawn. Some examples:\n   - #0008 is out. The chain is #0011 \u2190 #0026 \u2190 #0128 \u2190 #0939 \u2190 #1138. #1138 cancels #0939, which revives #0128. #0128 cancels #0026, which revives #0011, and #0011 removes #0008.\n   - #0298 is out. The chain runs #0317 \u2190 #0359 \u2190 #0540 \u2190 #0787 \u2190 #0813 \u2190 #1050 \u2190 #1088, and it ends with #0317 effective.\n   - #0039, #0017, #0061, #1217 and #1302 stand. In each case the withdrawal aimed at them was itself withdrawn.\n   - Single withdrawals remove their targets directly. Examples are #0005, #0010, #0057, #0321, #0565 and #1565.\n3. **Calculation.** I started from the $2,130K set in #0001. I then applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in record order. That gives a final budget of $1,287K.\n\nThis was a single pass by hand over about 1,600 records. I did not do a separate re-check.\n\nANSWER: $1287K",
